<%# Only the prompt is quoted in a bubble. The answer is the page speaking, so
    it takes the full column with nothing around it.

    `anchor` is optional: the thread stamps a message index on an entry so the
    entry can be linked to. `landed` is the other direction — this entry is the
    one a search result asked for, and the page scrolls here and rings it once.
    An entry with neither — the live turn, which has no stored index yet —
    simply carries no id and no mark. -%>
<% if role == "user" -%>
<div class="msg user<%= " is-landed" unless defined?(landed).nil? || !landed %>"<% if defined?(anchor) && anchor %> id="<%= h(anchor) %>"<% end %>>
  <div class="bubble text"><span class="sr-only">Kamu: </span><%= fmt_prompt(text) %></div>
</div>
<% else -%>
<div class="text"<% if defined?(anchor) && anchor %> id="<%= h(anchor) %>"<% end %>><span class="sr-only">Rubot: </span><%= fmt(text) %></div>
<% end -%>
